======================================================================================================
 (1) REAL CATALOG SPECS (recomputed from touched data; specs only -- estimator NOT fired on real data)
======================================================================================================
  Gannon+2024: 24 UDGs with stellar sigma (23 cluster/group = the 2026 reservoir);
    fractional sigma errors: median 0.24, range 0.06-0.46 (resampled in the MC)
    MEASURED astro floor: resid[ln sigma | ln M*, ln R_e] total 0.54 ln; measurement-subtracted
    INTRINSIC s_FJ(meas) = 0.48 ln (0.21 dex) -- vs banked 0.15: the in-hand
    heterogeneous population is x3.2 WORSE than the banked floor (24 objects, mixed
    distances/instruments/environments; if MI is true part of this scatter IS signal -> conservative).
  HeCS-omnibus: 227 clusters, median 180 members/cluster (sum 52415),
    median sigma_cl 686 km/s -- caustic membership + R200 per cluster (the free side).
  HeCS e_cz median 36 km/s vs sigma_cl 686 -> proxy k_r measurement noise 5% of sigma_cl:
    NEGLIGIBLE -- proxy dilution D is projection-dominated (banked D~0.4; D~0.6 with caustic zones), not noise.
  GalWCat19: 34471 members matched -> measured fraction in the 0.5-1.0 R200 shell = 0.40
    (members confined to <R200 by construction; the shell keeps ~40% of a targeted sample).

======================================================================================================
 (2) NULL CALIBRATION -- MG truth (f=0): the estimator's z must be standard normal, FP(3sig) ~ 1.3e-3
======================================================================================================
  MG-truth MC (N=400, 20k trials): mean z = -0.008, sd = 1.002, P(z>=3) = 0.0012 (expect ~0.0013)
  [OK] null calibrated: under ANY-MG truth the frozen estimator fires at 3 sigma with p~1.3e-3, as designed.
  sqrt(N) scaling check: z(800)/z(200) = 1.98 (expect 2.00)
  N_90 validation (fiducial f=10% can., ELT, s_FJ=0.15, D=0.4): N_90=2629 -> empirical power 0.91 (target 0.90)
  banked-analytic consistency: MC median-z N_3sigma = 1291 vs analytic two-bin 903 -> x1.43.
    EXPLAINED, BOTH WAYS: the analytic two-bin put the bins at the y-window ENDPOINTS (contrast = the
    full relational spread f); real settled/plunger CLASS MEANS sit inside the window (y~0.08 / y~1.35),
    so the usable contrast is ~85% of f -> N x~1.4. The MC is the honest number; the banked analytic
    was ~x1.4 optimistic ON TOP of its x2-5 FJ-floor correction. Same estimator, no free parameters.

